{
  "description": "Head coverage from newest windows (docs/message-sync.md#coverage, head spans). Each case starts from an empty file of `account` and runs `steps` in order: `events` are received (socket or query answer alike); `coverage` records a live or repair span `[from, to]` of `room`, captured now; `sent` marks a newest-window request going out for `rooms` under the name it gives (the mark is its capture); `head` is that request's answer (`sent` names the mark): `root` null for the room window, else the thread window of that root, `live_at` the time the live REQ carrying the room reached EOSE (the token's L), `has_more` and `next_cursor` from the answer's bounds, `ids` every event id the answer held. `token_changed: true` means the live token no longer held when the answer arrived: the client records no span (it only releases the mark). `forget_except` applies a membership list captured now; `lost` drops a receive (the file turns lossy). The relay's signing key `relay_key` is known, so its `history_changed` notices (40099) apply. The room window then reads `limit` rows of `kinds` (a thread window `limit` replies of `thread_kinds`) with the current EOSE time `live_at`. `expect` checks, when present: `room_certain`, `thread_certain`, `events` (every stored event id, sorted), `heads` (the head span per stream, `[lo_at, lo_id, hi_at]`, or null for none). Read by desktop (message_store/head_tests.rs) and mobile (message_store_head_test.dart).",
